00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.690
Infinity War Details
Ok so one of the best things about Infinity

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:12.280
War and Endgame as a whole is that the latter
pays off so many minor things in former that

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.260
the Russo Brother's should be applauded for
their sheer amount of attention to detail.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.940
Both movies were filmed back to back but even
so there are still some tiny little self-referential

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.970
things that show not only character detail
but also add to the world building.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:31.470
When talking to Doctor Strange, Tony Stark
and Wong, Bruce Banner is surprised to learn

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.750
that Ben and Jerry's have named an ice cream
flavour after him.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:38.570
This gets a big followup in Endgame when we
can see Hulk eating it during the planning

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:47.160
stages of the time heist.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.890
Also in Infinity War, Tony uses a nanotech
shield to cover himself from an attack by

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:52.890
Thanos.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.299
This severely depletes his supply of the microscopic
machines and leads to him being almost killed

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:58.460
by the Mad Titan.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:03.410
In order make sure this doesn't happen again,
in Endgame, Stark instead uses an Energy shield

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.619
as protection which won't put a drain on his
armour.

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:09.590
Clearly he has learned from his mistakes and
he's not the only one either.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.380
Throughout Infinity War after Thanos manages
to get his hands on two Infinity Stones, he

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.400
removes his armour, believing he is now invincible.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.260
However at the end of the movie the character
is almost killed by Thor and thus when he

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.079
makes his attack at the end of Endgame, the
younger version of the character realises

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:29.190
that it's probably sensible to keep his armour
on.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:32.739
Everytime Thor attacks the villain in the
film he goes for the head.

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:37.819
This was of course set up in Avengers: Infinity
War when due to his need to gloat he went

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:40.489
for his chest rather than an instant killing
blow.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:44.969
Because of this Thanos was able to wipe out
half of all life within the Galaxy and retreat

00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:46.099
to the garden.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:50.620
In Endgame he's here to kill him properly
this time and from their first meeting, all

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:55.639
the way until the final battle, everytime
Thor clashes with the character he aims directly

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:57.000
for his head.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.180
During this fight, we watch the awesome moment
in which Captain America lifts Mjlnoir and

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.790
gains the power of Thor.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:07.980
As Thanos cannot lift the item he instead
grabs Cap's wrists rather than the hammer

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:17.440
itself.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.459
Cap's armour has scales on it and you can
actually see these under the upper layer of

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:23.469
his outfit in Infinity War.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:27.780
These scales first made an appearance in Black
Panther and could show that after dropping

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.670
of Bucky in Wakanda, Shuri gave him some upgrades.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:35.340
Earlier in the film The Hulkbuster grabs Thanos
and you can see that the left arm on the armor

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.599
is unpainted.

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:40.309
This is because it was detached during the
final battle in the prior movie.

00:03:40.309 --> 00:03:42.999
Age Of Ultron
Thanos also breaks Cap's shield similar to

00:03:42.999 --> 00:03:46.959
the way that it was destroyed in Tony Stark's
vision all the way back in Age Of Ultron.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:50.069
Sacrifices
Infinity War was all about making sacrifices

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:51.109
in order to win.

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:55.409
Doctor Strange saved Tony in exchange for
handing over the time stone and there were

00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:57.560
several more examples of this in the film.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.099
I know this was part of his grand plan but
it still shows they put the few before the

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:03.099
many.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:06.819
Cap famously said that they don't trade lives
when Vision offered his life up in order to

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:10.959
destroy the mind stone and they wouldn't make
the hard play.

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:15.079
Thus Thanos was able to collect all of the
Infinity Stones and win.

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:18.280
This is because he was willing to sacrifice
Gamora.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:23.590
However, The Avengers win in Endgame because
they do make sacrifices including the death

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.460
of Black Widow and of course Tony Stark.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.500
Thematically it's amazing and really pays
off what was set up in the prior film.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.180
However, there are hints in Infinity War that
Gamora wasn't the first person to be sacrificed

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.590
for the Soul Stone.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:41.610
As she lays there dead at the bottom of the
ravine we can see a pool of blood beside her.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.460
Could this be Natasha's from 2014?

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.389
Well we do know that she did trade her life
and then Cap returned the Soul Stone so therefore

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.810
this moment would be permanent and it wouldn't
cause a branched timeline.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:57.770
The blood isn't there when Natasha dies and
it would still remain after she perished.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:02.090
Could it be that the Russo brothers were foreshadowing
Natashas death in Endgame during this moment

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.629
in the preceding film?

00:05:04.629 --> 00:05:05.720
I think so.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.349
When Natasha tells Steve that she has to work
on fixing everything the soundtrack is also

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:14.810
a variation on the Soul Stone sacrifice music
which foreshadows her death later.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.330
Returning The Stones
When Steve sets out on his mission to return

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.259
the stones he says to Bucky.

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:22.069
“Don’t do anything stupid until I get
back."

00:05:22.069 --> 00:05:24.060
Bucky replies
“How can I?

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:28.300
You’re taking all the stupid with you,”
This is actually a callback to Captain America:

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.870
The First Avenger in which the conversation
was reversed with Steve delivering the opposite

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.330
dialogue to Bucky before he went off to fight
in World War 2.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:39.910
Before leaving on his mission, Cap looks in
the direction of where his old version would

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.680
later be sat and says 'I'll be back.'

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.120
At the end of the film Steve and Peggy finally
get that dance and it's the same song from

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.289
when Steve found fury in his apartment in
the winter soldier.

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:54.780
The song is called 'It's been a long long
time' which is of course a reference to the

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.460
journey that Steve has been on to finally
get his long lost love.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.259
When taking the Pym Particles from Hank, he
takes four in total.

00:06:02.259 --> 00:06:06.530
This is two for him and Stark to return to
the present and one for him to go to the past

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.870
and another to eventually return to the present.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:14.310
After returning from the past on his own little
journey Hawkeye seems pretty beat.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:19.180
Scott grabs some orange slices which is a
call back to Civil War in which he asked if

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.539
anyone had any to help ease his pain.

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:25.810
Natasha makes a Peanut Butter Jelly sandwich
which Scott then shows up and eats.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:30.169
She cuts it diagonally which is a call back
to Nick Fury telling Carol that he can't eat

00:06:30.169 --> 00:06:32.490
toast that's been cut diagonally.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.930
Could she be in the habit of doing this to
stop Nick from stealing her lunch at work?

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:37.980
We'd like to think so.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.970
Thor Ragnarok
That's not the only neat little easter egg

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:42.780
that ties into other movies in the MCU.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:48.090
In Thor Ragnarok before Odin Dies he says
to Thor and his brother 'remember this place,

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.090
home.'

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.170
This scene takes place in Norway and is actually
the location that New Asgard would come to

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.499
be in Endgame.

00:06:54.499 --> 00:06:57.250
But it's not the only time the area makes
a big appearance.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:02.310
Tonsberg has been a crucial location in the
MCU from the beginning.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.379
This is the location where the Asgardians
fought centuries ago, it's also where the

00:07:06.379 --> 00:07:11.319
tesseract was hidden and then taken by Red
Skull and it is of course where Odin dies

00:07:11.319 --> 00:07:17.210
and New Asgard comes to be.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:21.430
During Ragnarok a line is also set up and
paid off in Endgame.

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:25.280
Loki tells Thor that he cannot see into the
future as he's not a witch.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:30.400
In Endgame Frigga can tell that Thor is from
the future because as she says she was 'raised

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.400
by Witches.'

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.400
This implies that Witches can tell the future
in the MCU and I love the way it references

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.400
this line from the third Thor film.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:34.400
Tony And His Dad
It's not the only touching exchange between

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.389
parent and child son that has major callbacks
to the MCU either and in Endgame when Howard

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:42.560
asks Tony about his father, Stark Junior says
'He did his best.'

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.800
This is a nod to the BARF demonstration in
Civil War in which Tony shows that he wishes

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.259
he told his father 'I love you dad, and I
know you did the best you could'.

00:07:51.259 --> 00:07:52.800
I'm not crying.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.830
You're crying!

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.229
During this scene Jarvis from Agent Carter
pops up too.

00:07:57.229 --> 00:08:00.379
I know you've probably heard that one a hundred
times I just wanted to add it in.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.749
Avengers
There's tonnes of call back too and loads

00:08:02.749 --> 00:08:07.509
of nice little easter eggs in the scene in
which Tony and Scott go to Stark Tower in

00:08:07.509 --> 00:08:08.509
2012.

00:08:08.509 --> 00:08:12.560
Tony's armor retracts from the feet first
to silence his landing and make it so they

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.849
aren't heard entering the room.

00:08:13.849 --> 00:08:17.509
Thor says that they're going for lunch which
is a reference to the Schwarma scene from

00:08:17.509 --> 00:08:19.539
the post credits scene of the film.

00:08:19.539 --> 00:08:24.819
Tony also flicks Ant-Man with insane accuracy
because he'd been practicing playing Paper

00:08:24.819 --> 00:08:26.879
Football with Nebula for weeks.

00:08:26.879 --> 00:08:30.840
When exiting the building, Tony replays a
similar move to which he did in the first

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:35.770
Avengers movie, however his suit quickly engages
over him instead of when he almost hits the

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:39.430
pavement which shows how far his technology
has come since 2012.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:43.270
The Quantum Suits
Speaking of technology the Quantum suits themselves

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.330
also show the melding of a lot of the tech
in the MCU.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:50.850
They use Pym tech in order to shrink, the
Nano Tech is from Iron-Man and Wakanda's nano

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.810
machines and the visor is from the Guardians
and Ratchet...sorry I mean Rocket.

00:08:55.810 --> 00:09:00.060
Speaking of Ratchet, Tony calls him this in
the film and it's a reference to the furry

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.560
Sony character who is also great with machines.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.800
Community Cast
The Russos love casting people from their

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.420
previous work and Anthony Russo's daughter
plays Hawkeyes in the film.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.500
This is who he is seen training in the beginning
and you may notice sounds of birds and wildlife

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.940
in the background.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:18.850
After the snap is carried out these disappear
showing that a lot of animals were also killed

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:20.880
when Thanos carried out the devastating move.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:24.820
The child we see in Captain America: The Winter
Soldier also returns to take a picture with

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:26.500
Smart Hulk at the diner scene.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:30.760
Two community actors also pop up including
Yvette Nicole Brown who gets in a lift with

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.760
Steve and Tony and also Ken Jeong who is a
guard at the lock-up.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.020
Jeong is reading a book called Terminal Breach
which is about a President who decides to

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:43.070
destroy countless nuclear weapons at the cost
of millions of lives.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:46.960
This of course has ties to Thanos' plan in
which he killed trillions in order to save

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:47.960
the Galaxy.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:48.960
The lockup Ant-Man is in is 616 which is a
reference to the main Marvel universe which

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:49.960
also carries this designation.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:50.960
Final Battle
Spider-Man told Tony in Civil War that he'd

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:54.590
never get a chance to play football due to
his powers but we see him get the opportunity

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:58.310
in the final battle in which the character
literally runs the guantlet.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:02.540
In Spider-man: Homecoming there's a hilarious
scene in which Peter thought Tony was going

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:03.660
for a hug.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.740
Tony says "We're not there yet".

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:19.000
but in "Endgame" Tony and Peter hug which
shows how far their friendship 

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.870
has come.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:26.710
You can also see Peter's traditional Spider-man
costume under the suit when it's damaged.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:31.600
This is because he had it on under the Iron-Spider
Armour all the way back in Infinity War.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.600
As he died on Titan and then came straight
to the final battle after being ressurected

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:36.730
he wouldn't have had time to change.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:37.730
The final battle has tonnes of tiny little
things in it that you may miss if you're not

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:38.730
playing close attention.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:42.250
When War Machine is stuck in Avengers HQ he
gets out the suit by saying 'canopy, canopy,

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:46.280
canopy' which is code for 'eject, eject, eject'
in the air force.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:50.210
A pilot says this to their backseater so they
can leave first.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.470
You can also see Iron Patriot Mark 2 Armor
in the background of this scene which makes

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:55.500
an appearance later on.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.500
When fighting Thanos Cap throws the shield
and then the hammer at the shield which knocks

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:57.500
Thanos off balance and is a callback to when
the two struck one another in Avengers.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.760
The Wasp exists a tiny small portal and we
also see Spider-man swinging on Ant-Man in

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.320
order to move forward.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:07.270
The end of the film culminates with Tony carrying
out the snap and killing Thanos and his forces.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:11.760
Not only can you hear Tony's Nano machines
taking the stones of Thanos' gauntlet and

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:16.380
putting them into his suit but there are also
a couple of neat little callbacks to the prior

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.380
film.

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:21.680
the first time we hear Thanos talk in Infinity
War he says he knows what it's like to lose

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.860
and how it turns the legs to jelly.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:27.060
When dying, the first thing he does is sit
down.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:31.380
Why this scene is also perfect is because
the camera movement mimics his victory at

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.470
the end of Avengers Infinity War.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:38.720
It pans across exactly the same way and show
the victory and defeat in a similar light.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:41.200
Tony's funeral
At Tony's funeral everyone rocks back and

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.950
forth except for Mantis who sways in a rocking
motion.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:49.250
This was put in place because it's typical
of Mantids to sway when stood still.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:53.850
Morgan tells Happy that she wants some cheeseburgers
and this is a reference to the first Iron-Man

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:58.300
in which Tony made Happy get him some cheeseburgers
after returning home from being held hostage.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:02.490
The credits ends with the clanging noise of
Iron-Man building his suit in the first film

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.260
and this brings everything full circle.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:10.640
All 22 films which is also paid lip service
to by Stark in the beginning of Endgame who

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:14.060
says they've been adrift for 21 days...no
22.

